  "description": "The STARTBR refusal at :612-618, forced onto the positioning probe because twelve well-formed records cannot make a positioning request fail - the arm has to be reached deliberately or not at all. It is the only one of the three STARTBR arms that sets WS-ERR-FLG (:614, against the bare CONTINUE at :603 and the end-of-data arm at :605-611 that sets TRANSACT-EOF instead), and that one byte reshapes the whole of PROCESS-PAGE-FORWARD: the guard at :283 is false, so the skip-read at :285-287, the blanking loop at :290-292, the paging loop at :297-303, both page-number COMPUTE sites at :306-307 and :317-318, all three next-page SETs at :310, :312 and :315, ENDBR at :322, MOVE CDEMO-CT00-PAGE-NUM TO PAGENUMI at :324, MOVE SPACE TO TRNIDINO at :325 and the SEND at :326 are every one of them bypassed. What this case pins is therefore an ABSENCE: the probe is the only read the browse ever serves, no READNEXT and no READPREV follow it, and :322 is never reached - so a translation that walked the browse anyway, or that ended one it had never positioned, fails here instead of passing quietly. Nothing is written, because the program has no WRITE, REWRITE or DELETE to reach. The page number stays at the zero :224 moved into it and the next-page flag stays at the N :99 set, since both sites that would have moved them sit inside the bypassed block. TWO sends are expected, not one: the failure arm's own at :618, and MAIN-PARA's unconditional one at :116 which the first-entry branch performs after PROCESS-ENTER-KEY. Both carry ERASE, because this arm never disturbs the flag :100 set - unlike the PF7 and PF8 refusals at :250 and :272, which are the only two paths that flip it. Back in PROCESS-ENTER-KEY the guard at :227 is false as well, so MOVE SPACE TO TRNIDINO at :228 does not run either; on this path it would have overwritten the LOW-VALUES :114 already left there, which is why the site matters to the branch rather than to the bytes. The DISPLAY of RESP and RESP2 at :613 is a log line and not a terminal line, so it is not an emitted message here; what is emitted is 'Unable to lookup transaction...' from :615-616, space-padded to the eighty bytes WS-MESSAGE declares at :38 and then right-truncated to the seventy-eight ERRMSGO carries, which is exactly the MOVE at :531. No attribute value is expected anywhere: COTRN00C copies DFHBMSCA at :81 and never uses it and does not copy CSSETATY at all, so a failure shows itself in the message text and the flags and never in a colour byte. The class is called TransactionMenuController, but the program header at :5 reads 'List Transactions from TRANSACT file' and this is that list screen's refusal path, not a menu's - the mandated name is honoured and the behaviour is taken from the source. Every value here was derived by reading app/cbl/COTRN00C.cbl against app/cpy/CVTRA05Y.cpy (the 350-byte record, FILLER X(20) included), app/cpy-bms/COTRN00.CPY, app/cpy/COCOM01Y.cpy and app/csd/CARDDEMO.CSD; none of it was captured from a running COBOL program, because no COBOL can be run in this environment.",
